  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For a compound to be aromatic it must have $(4 n+2) \\pi e^{-}$and system should be planar where $n$ is an integer. (V) and (VI) both have $4 e^{-}$and planar structure. Hence are Antiaromatic",
    "image": null
